@startuml sequence_diagram_camera_interaction
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - VIS07 Pan, Orbit, Dolly, Reset View and Per-Frame Limits

actor User as "LaPrizza Manager"
participant Viewer as "KitchenViewer\n(Reset view button)"
participant Canvas as "Canvas\n(domElement)"
participant Orbit as "OrbitControls"
participant Ctrl as "CameraController"
participant Limits as "cameraLimits"
participant Clamp as "clampTarget"
participant Engine as "ViewerEngine\n(frame loop)"
participant Three as "three\n(PerspectiveCamera / WebGLRenderer)"

note over User, Three
    Precondition: state "ready" (sequence_diagram_camera_init).
    Listeners are on the canvas only: input over the VIS06 GUI, toolbar or menus
    never moves the camera. Mouse events only change the OrbitControls state;
    limits are applied and the view is rendered in the next frame (section 5).
end note

== 1. Pan (left button + drag) ==

User -> Canvas : left button down + drag
activate Canvas
Canvas -> Orbit : pointerdown / pointermove (LEFT = PAN)
activate Orbit
Orbit -> Orbit : accumulate pan on the floor plane (y = 0)
Orbit --> Canvas : event handled
deactivate Orbit
Canvas --> User : pan applied (and clamped) on the next frame
deactivate Canvas

== 2. Orbit (right button + drag) ==

User -> Canvas : right button down + drag
activate Canvas
Canvas -> Orbit : contextmenu (suppressed); pointermove (RIGHT = ROTATE)
activate Orbit
Orbit -> Orbit : accumulate rotation around the current target
Orbit --> Canvas : event handled
deactivate Orbit
Canvas --> User : orbit applied on the next frame\n(polar [5, 85] deg; azimuth free)
deactivate Canvas

== 3. Dolly (mouse wheel) ==

User -> Canvas : wheel up / down
activate Canvas
Canvas -> Orbit : wheel (DOLLY); preventDefault: page does not scroll
activate Orbit
Orbit -> Orbit : accumulate dolly towards / away from the target;\nFOV unchanged (50 deg), zoomToCursor = false
Orbit --> Canvas : event handled
deactivate Orbit
Canvas --> User : dolly applied on the next frame\n(distance [0.5 m, maxDistance])
deactivate Canvas

== 4. Reset view (also during inertia) ==

User -> Viewer : clicks "Reset view"
activate Viewer
Viewer -> Canvas : dispatchEvent("kitchen-viewer:reset-view")
activate Canvas
Canvas -> Ctrl : onResetView()
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Ctrl : resetView() -> applyInitialView()
Ctrl -> Orbit : flushMomentum(): enableDamping = false; update();\nenableDamping = true
activate Orbit
Orbit --> Ctrl : residual inertia discarded
deactivate Orbit
Ctrl -> Three : camera.position = initialView.position
activate Three
Three --> Ctrl : position set
deactivate Three
Ctrl -> Orbit : target.set(0, 0, 0); update()
activate Orbit
Orbit --> Ctrl : initial view restored
deactivate Orbit
Ctrl --> Canvas : done
deactivate Ctrl
Canvas --> Viewer : event handled
deactivate Canvas
Viewer --> User : initial view of the current layout,\nno residual movement
deactivate Viewer
note right of Ctrl
    Native controls.reset() is NOT used: it keeps the
    damping momentum and the camera would keep drifting
    after the reset (D10).
end note

== 5. Every frame (limits and smooth movement) ==

loop each animation frame
    Engine -> Ctrl : update(dt)  (through CameraControlsModule)
    activate Engine
    activate Ctrl
    Ctrl -> Three : read camera.aspect
    activate Three
    Three --> Ctrl : aspect
    deactivate Three
    alt aspect != lastAspect (canvas resized by VIS01)
        Ctrl -> Limits : computeCameraLimits(dimensions, aspect, wall)
        activate Limits
        Limits --> Ctrl : new fitDistance, maxDistance, far
        deactivate Limits
        Ctrl -> Orbit : applyLimits(): maxDistance = limits.maxDistance
        Ctrl -> Three : far = limits.far; updateProjectionMatrix()
        activate Three
        Three --> Ctrl : projection updated
        deactivate Three
        opt distance to target > maxDistance
            Ctrl -> Three : move camera closer along the SAME direction
            activate Three
            Three --> Ctrl : view preserved
            deactivate Three
        end
        Ctrl -> Ctrl : lastAspect = aspect
    end
    Ctrl -> Orbit : update()  (damping 0.08)
    activate Orbit
    Orbit -> Three : camera position / orientation
    activate Three
    Three --> Orbit : camera updated
    deactivate Three
    Orbit --> Ctrl : updated
    deactivate Orbit
    Ctrl -> Clamp : clampTarget(target, camera.position, targetBounds)
    activate Clamp
    alt target inside x in [-w/2, w/2], z in [-d/2, d/2]
        Clamp --> Ctrl : false (nothing changed)
    else target outside the floor rectangle
        Clamp -> Clamp : clamp target x/z;\nmove camera by the same correction
        Clamp --> Ctrl : true
        Ctrl -> Orbit : flushMomentum()
        activate Orbit
        Orbit --> Ctrl : residual pan discarded
        deactivate Orbit
        Ctrl -> Clamp : clampTarget(...) again
        Clamp --> Ctrl : target and camera on the boundary
    end
    deactivate Clamp
    Ctrl --> Engine : done
    deactivate Ctrl
    Engine -> Three : render(scene, camera)
    activate Three
    Three --> Engine : frame rendered
    deactivate Three
    Engine --> User : updated view shown on the canvas
    deactivate Engine
end

note over Ctrl, Engine
    The pan limit does not depend on the OrbitControls "change" event, which is
    not emitted for movements below its internal threshold: the clamp runs on
    EVERY frame, before render. Discarding the momentum at the boundary makes a
    reversed drag respond immediately. CameraController is the single writer of
    the camera (BR 8); no allocation per frame. Speeds 0.5 / 0.8 / 0.6.
end note
@enduml